VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  The reduced (Theta, chi) Dirac block was fine as far as it went; the lapse was not in it.  Once the coupling d chi . d ln N is
  put into the ADM action, integrating out chi leaves a k-dependent lapse term, the lapse stops being a Lagrange multiplier, and
  the curvature perturbation acquires a kinetic term A = lam a k^2 W/(4H^2) with NO gradient term: one extra scalar, dust-like
  (c_s^2 = 0, the mimetic class), absent in GR (A_GR = 0).  By the proposal's own rule
  ('if the full Hamiltonian analysis reveals a propagating mode, we kill it immediately') the branch-selective filter, as written,
  is a dark field by another name.  The large-scale fix of the growth gate stands as a target for a construction that filters the
  MOND enhancement without a lapse-gradient coupling -- that construction does not yet exist.

